.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PCI_SCAN 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pci_scan_bus
.Nd scan one PCI bus for functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/pci.h
.Ft int
.Fn pci_scan_bus "uint8_t bus"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pci_scan_bus
function iterates over slots 0 through 31 on the specified PCI bus.
For each populated slot, it probes function 0 and inspects the header-type
multifunction bit.
Single-function devices are scanned only at function 0.
Multifunction devices are scanned across functions 0 through 7.
.Pp
Each discovered function is recorded in the kernel PCI device list and is made
available through
.Fn pci_find_device .
.Pp
On systems without PCI configuration mechanism #1, the scan is skipped and no
devices are recorded.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn pci_scan_bus
function returns the number of functions discovered on the requested bus.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pci_config 9 ,
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr driver 9
